    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619681469311_688191_90953" xmi:uuid="3f9e1260-9b25-4c5f-b999-83281b2a5097" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620293007332_698291_94242" xmi:uuid="a6533b2b-bdda-4126-ad95-022aa96d7d14" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619681469311_688191_90953"/>
        <body>An AnnotatedModelItemAssociation is an identification of a Callout within an AnnotatedModelPresentation as being the element that describes a GeometricDimension, GeometricTolerance, ShapeFeatureDefinition, ShapeElement or a ShapeElementRelationship. &lt;example&gt;In an application protocol, an instance of GeometricModel describes a characteristic of a product. One element of the GeometricModel - a Curve - represents the boundary of a hole that is a ShapeElement in the product. This entity data type may be used to state that the curve describes the hole, in the context of the entire GeometricModel describing the shape of the product.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>AnnotatedModelItemAssociation</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721221106975_413699_148773" xmi:uuid="d0268caf-496d-4f44-aec9-011e921b675e" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general href="../ManagementResources/ManagementResources.xmi#_18_4_1_65b021e_1719937607582_594298_150024"/>
      </generalization>
