    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510892129_23236_94760" xmi:uuid="90012275-cdd2-413b-b697-d4fedad65758" xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619511017090_68131_94789" xmi:uuid="55a990ee-2823-4309-bf54-4ed2fe7681d5" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510892129_23236_94760"/>
        <body>The AnnotationPlaceholderOccurrenceRole is either a user defined text or a class of geometric product specification. </body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>AnnotationPlaceholderOccurrenceRoleEnum</name>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510939109_868881_94783" xmi:uuid="7815fb2a-415b-4f3e-a523-c00416c450c2" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510956005_131939_94785" xmi:uuid="c8cb1e2e-f95a-4c7c-8c3b-f42cc0dc0345" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510939109_868881_94783"/>
          <body>user defined text.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>annotation_text</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510963701_210747_94786" xmi:uuid="25f8bec2-5f0b-49f9-8d40-78b378702c4c" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510974963_253190_94788" xmi:uuid="bcee9c47-4672-40c6-b0c4-ceea01a7483a" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619510963701_210747_94786"/>
          <body>geometric product specification class that associated with a specific entity type in this document. </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>gps_data</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206299307_292407_99265" xmi:uuid="9339cd7d-78a7-4d54-be77-91c9f991e4d8" xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620301912324_640012_91690" xmi:uuid="7c4b8aa6-c0b6-46ca-a10a-9ddb34b81f34" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206299307_292407_99265"/>
        <body>The LeaderLinePointSymbolEnum provides an identification of the required symbol to be used in a specific segment of a leader line. &lt;note&gt;The actual graphic of the symbol is not provided, but the interpretation shall be in accordance with applicable draughting standards.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>LeaderLinePointSymbolEnum</name>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206438639_647132_99314" xmi:uuid="cedc8814-6a8d-4129-906d-5248df967065" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620302092876_685877_91691" xmi:uuid="2684d739-e4a4-442a-a99a-c67416345d6d" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206438639_647132_99314"/>
          <body>a circle is to be applied to the point specified in the leader line. &lt;note&gt;The Figure &lt;caption&gt;A LeaderLine circle as an "as provided" example&lt;/caption&gt; illustrates the 'as provided' data for the application of a circle to a leader line. The point list for figure &lt;caption&gt;A LeaderLine circle as an "as provided" example&lt;/caption&gt; is (A1, A2, A3).&lt;/note&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;annotaion_to_model_leader_line_circle_as_provided.gif&lt;/name&gt;A LeaderLine circle as an "as provided" example&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;note&gt;The Figure &lt;caption&gt;A LeaderLine circle as an "as rendered" example&lt;/caption&gt; illustrates the 'as rendered' presentation for the application of a circle to a leader line. The point list for Figure &lt;caption&gt;A LeaderLine circle as an "as rendered" example&lt;/caption&gt; is (A1, A2, A3).&lt;/note&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;annotaion_to_model_leader_line_circle_as_rendered.gif&lt;/name&gt;A LeaderLine circle as an "as rendered" example&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>circle</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206450573_677040_99316" xmi:uuid="7efaee88-8b48-4716-9629-8ffed9f5b775" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620302099701_743287_91692" xmi:uuid="34861454-aa16-4b38-9094-73afce4c18ae" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206450573_677040_99316"/>
          <body>a dot is to be applied to the point specified in the leader line.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>dot</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206459354_526517_99318" xmi:uuid="5f57d3bb-3d16-4336-8fdd-ad1f09cdb55a" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620302116037_722411_91693" xmi:uuid="6234a4e7-01ed-42ab-a3b5-433ecb01b184" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206459354_526517_99318"/>
          <body>an internal_pair_forward_arrowhead is one end of a pair of arrows where there is no annotation between the arrows. Forward is to be interpreted as the leader line arrives to the point. The arrowhead is at a point with an index in the list of points that is greater than the point to which the internal_pair_reverse_arrowhead is applied. &lt;note&gt;The Figure &lt;caption&gt;An LeaderLine arrowhead pair as an "as rendered" example&lt;/caption&gt; illustrates the 'as rendered' presentation for the application of both the internal pair forward and reverse arrowheads to a leader line. The point list for the Figure &lt;caption&gt;An LeaderLine arrowhead pair as an "as rendered" example&lt;/caption&gt; is (B1, B2, B3, B4).&lt;/note&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;annotation_to_model_leader_line_arrowhead_pair_as_rendered.gif&lt;/name&gt;An LeaderLine arrowhead pair as an "as rendered" example&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>internal_pair_forward_arrowhead</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206471714_356198_99320" xmi:uuid="3203fef7-922a-4dc4-b30f-b1f475e1551b" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620302837318_36124_91709" xmi:uuid="a7028ab9-c86d-44b7-a54c-a48de236b426" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206471714_356198_99320"/>
          <body>an internal_pair_reverse_arrowhead is one end of a pair of arrows where there is no annotation between the arrows. Reverse is to be interpreted as the leader line leaves the point. The arrowhead is at a point with an index in the list of points that is less than the point to which the internal_pair_forward_arrowhead is applied.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>internal_pair_reverse_arrowhead</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206481309_200955_99322" xmi:uuid="d1754503-067f-40f7-862d-c3976c0bf6c3" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620302844442_77170_91710" xmi:uuid="b66a4c5b-ac64-438f-b125-598d194128dc" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206481309_200955_99322"/>
          <body>there is no symbol applied.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>none</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206491788_438603_99324" xmi:uuid="e46491bf-92f9-4520-8133-a2bec4aaf7ef" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620302853154_695293_91711" xmi:uuid="1107169f-7fea-4e7e-ade3-898a544ed79d" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206491788_438603_99324"/>
          <body>a positive_arrowhead is applied to a point where the index of the point in the list of points is greater than the index of the first point in the list.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>positive_arrowhead</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206500796_31677_99326" xmi:uuid="489d8d0a-64aa-4bac-9362-cfb576bbfaa5" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620302862019_14226_91712" xmi:uuid="e4502605-5428-4ebd-9ca0-e3bcdf0a0855" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620206500796_31677_99326"/>
          <body> a triangle is applied to a point where the index of the point in the list of points is greater than the index of the first point in the list.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>triangle</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619516088698_44291_95098" xmi:uuid="939b8e01-9f43-457d-88a4-d85dbc002b52" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620028579608_160442_91631" xmi:uuid="34c5a87c-473b-4417-b89d-92ebe7c30cb3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619516088698_44291_95098"/>
        <body>An AnnotatedModelPresentation is a type of StyledModel that describes a presentation of model with annotation according to ISO 16792.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>AnnotatedModelPresentation</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1682327407604_872084_153369" xmi:uuid="32baeced-7c33-46e6-93ee-ab0ff0d53c30" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1682327439079_98279_153371" xmi:uuid="844b5103-d345-4c4f-9fe5-cc5aa4b335e7" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1682327407604_872084_153369"/>
          <body>If the PresentationType is 'Saved View', Items shall contain exactly one CameraModel3D.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1682327498190_736875_153381" xmi:uuid="c32e4dde-8479-4fe8-b489-557e13d9de99" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1682327509118_992789_153382" xmi:uuid="30937eda-9261-426f-8172-192ebd0949fd" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>&lt;sch:rule context="//Representation[ @uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='AnnotatedModelPresentation' and ./PresentationType/ClassString='Saved View']"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uidRef" value="./Items/RepresentationItem/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test=" count (//RepresentationItem[substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='CameraModel3D' and @uid=$uidRef]) = 1 "&gt; (AnnotatedModelPresentation.WR2: &lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt;) If the PresentationType is 'Saved View', the Items shall contain exactly one CameraModel3D. &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR2</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619516088698_44291_95098"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1682327407605_890146_153370" xmi:uuid="58250de4-f347-4331-931b-568970c6b7e0" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.PresentationType.oclAsType(Application_protocols::AP242::Domain_model::CommonResources::ClassStringProxy).value= 'Saved View' implies (self.Items -&gt; select(oclIsKindOf(Application_protocols::AP242::Domain_model::AnnotatedModelPresentation::CameraModel3D))) -&gt; size() = 1</body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1649421720450_652623_151520" xmi:uuid="cec32753-21dc-4413-b75c-445b224de473" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1649421781525_267601_151530" xmi:uuid="a66ca4d6-6b04-4bb6-829e-534430139e78" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1649421720450_652623_151520"/>
          <body>the name should be unique within a population of the AnnotatedModelPresentation.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1651571820746_314728_147955" xmi:uuid="bd332058-3f1f-4076-8cda-ce9e90e10de3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1651571841811_607340_147958" xmi:uuid="0038adb8-68a4-46ba-b52e-d5cd4672ba15" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>&lt;sch:rule context="//Representation[ @uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='AnnotatedModelPresentation']"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="name" value="./Name/CharacterString"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="not($name = following-sibling::Representation[substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='AnnotatedModelPresentation']/Name/CharacterString or $name = preceding-sibling::Representation[substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='AnnotatedModelPresentation']/Name/CharacterString)"&gt; (AnnotatedModelPresentation.WR1 &lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt;) the name should be unique within a population of the AnnotatedModelPresentation/&gt; &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619516088698_44291_95098"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1649421720456_737808_151521" xmi:uuid="d609cb58-07d9-4847-be44-8d8d0b20727b" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>AnnotatedModelPresentation::allInstances()-&gt;isUnique( Name.oclAsType(Application_protocols::AP242::Domain_model::CommonResources::Descriptor).Text.oclAsType(Application_protocols::AP242::Domain_model::CommonResources::CharacterStringProxy).value )</body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619612199767_158507_91094" xmi:uuid="661cac78-fd48-4339-b71f-554ee9bb4787" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general href="../RepresentationAndExternalElementReference/RepresentationAndExternalElementReference.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193257_299866_23863"/>
      </generalization>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619595504556_244226_90773" xmi:uuid="cfa000ea-4a43-41a6-9bfe-b21a229419e0" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619595504556_305407_90775" xmi:uuid="482d89ae-b68e-4049-937a-3a1ec50a988c" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619595504556_244226_90773"/>
          <body>the instances of RepresentationItem that are included in the Representation. </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>Items</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619595333854_639499_90730"/>
        <upperValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1619595504556_266653_90774" xmi:uuid="897ad908-ea81-476d-a62d-ed209bf3a76d" xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
          <value>*</value>
        </upperValue>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1619686920706_458084_91443"/>
        <redefinedProperty href="../RepresentationAndExternalElementReference/RepresentationAndExternalElementReference.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194007_289896_28693"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620046515253_558629_92936" xmi:uuid="ba34c0f1-ae01-4c02-9693-b5c81288cf18" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620046569976_412279_92942" xmi:uuid="cb44b509-025f-476a-8f6d-223e6c04ca09" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1620046515253_558629_92936"/>
          <body>specifies the type of presentation. &lt;note&gt; The type 'Global Draughting Model' is used for the AnnotatedModelPresentation that contains all AnnotationElements, Callouts, CameraModel3D and StyledModelReplication.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt; The type 'Saved View' is used for saved views according to ISO 16792. A saved view shall have an identifier, contain exactly one CameraModel3D that denotes the direction of the view relative to the model, and may contain one or more of the AnnotationPlane(s), a selected set of annotation, or a selected set of geometry.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>PresentationType</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193042_855579_23449"/>
        <upperValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1620046540078_457717_92941" xmi:uuid="48c2e7bb-95e2-4a56-8726-006df67327c3" xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
          <value>*</value>
        </upperValue>
      </ownedAttribute>
    </packagedElement>
